WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.166 --> 00:00:01.401
Our houses were demolished.

00:00:01.401 --> 00:00:02.902
There was no building left.

00:00:02.902 --> 00:00:04.337
Whole cities were flattened.

00:00:04.337 --> 00:00:05.772
Everything disappeared.

00:00:05.772 --> 00:00:07.273
We can feed our souls here,

00:00:07.273 --> 00:00:08.041
but no one knows

00:00:08.041 --> 00:00:10.210
how we're going to live much

00:00:10.210 --> 00:00:10.977
It's freezing,

00:00:10.977 --> 00:00:12.746
and we will be frozen to death here.

00:00:12.746 --> 00:00:14.280
If we sit inside the tent,

00:00:14.280 --> 00:00:15.782
we will freeze.

00:00:16.049 --> 00:00:16.950
Those are the stories

00:00:16.950 --> 00:00:17.884
that we are hearing from

00:00:17.884 --> 00:00:18.985
some of the survivors

00:00:18.985 --> 00:00:19.552
about a week

00:00:19.552 --> 00:00:22.055
after the 7.8 magnitude earthquake

00:00:22.322 --> 00:00:24.491
leveled parts of Syria and Turkey,

00:00:24.491 --> 00:00:26.760
leaving so many people in despair

00:00:26.793 --> 00:00:27.727
with major questions

00:00:27.727 --> 00:00:29.162
now about what to do.

00:00:29.162 --> 00:00:31.998
More than 36,000 people have died

00:00:31.998 --> 00:00:33.166
and the toll is continuing

00:00:33.166 --> 00:00:33.767
to rise

00:00:33.767 --> 00:00:34.234
as aid

00:00:34.234 --> 00:00:36.936
and rescue efforts are underway here.

00:00:36.936 --> 00:00:37.370
A nine year

00:00:37.370 --> 00:00:37.771
old boy

00:00:37.771 --> 00:00:39.305
was pulled from the ruins

00:00:39.305 --> 00:00:41.408
of a collapsed building on Sunday.

00:00:41.408 --> 00:00:42.442
This father and daughter

00:00:42.442 --> 00:00:43.510
were rescued out of the rubble,

00:00:43.510 --> 00:00:45.879
still alive in Turkey.

00:00:46.279 --> 00:00:47.947
All of this is coming as criticism

00:00:47.947 --> 00:00:49.082
and anger is building

00:00:49.082 --> 00:00:49.983
towards the government

00:00:49.983 --> 00:00:51.084
and President Erdogan

00:00:51.084 --> 00:00:52.819
of their handling of the crisis.

00:00:52.819 --> 00:00:53.553
Even Erdogan

00:00:53.553 --> 00:00:55.088
acknowledging that the government's

00:00:55.088 --> 00:00:57.290
initial response was slow.

00:00:57.290 --> 00:00:57.991
CNN's Sara

00:00:57.991 --> 00:01:00.160
Sidner is live in southern Turkey.

00:01:00.160 --> 00:01:01.895
Sara, I know we were talking earlier

00:01:01.895 --> 00:01:02.762
the rescue efforts

00:01:02.762 --> 00:01:03.663
were very much underway.

00:01:03.663 --> 00:01:04.597
The recovery efforts

00:01:04.597 --> 00:01:05.465
of all of this debris

00:01:05.465 --> 00:01:06.633
that you're seeing behind the scenes.

00:01:06.633 --> 00:01:08.134
Is even hard to breathe

00:01:08.134 --> 00:01:10.236
because there's so much smoke in the air.

00:01:10.236 --> 00:01:11.504
What are you hearing from people

00:01:14.974 --> 00:01:15.575
You know,

00:01:15.575 --> 00:01:16.076
the moment

00:01:16.076 --> 00:01:16.342
that we

00:01:16.342 --> 00:01:17.243
got on the ground,

00:01:17.243 --> 00:01:18.445
just within moments

00:01:18.445 --> 00:01:19.879
of stopping and getting out of a car,

00:01:19.879 --> 00:01:21.281
we were approached

00:01:21.281 --> 00:01:22.315
by a woman

00:01:22.315 --> 00:01:24.417
who was begging us to help her

00:01:24.417 --> 00:01:26.386
find her husband.

00:01:26.386 --> 00:01:28.755
The sorrow is so palpable here.

00:01:29.022 --> 00:01:31.291
That is what you notice first.

00:01:31.291 --> 00:01:33.259
Then you see the amount of destruction

00:01:33.259 --> 00:01:34.294
and it really is

00:01:34.294 --> 00:01:36.563
hard to get your mind around it.

00:01:38.598 --> 00:01:39.065
Oh,

00:01:39.966 --> 00:01:41.201
yes, sure.

00:01:41.201 --> 00:01:42.435
Yes, you

00:01:43.103 --> 00:01:44.971
do, because it's

00:01:44.971 --> 00:01:47.907
the 38 year old Code Red Coachbuilder

00:01:48.141 --> 00:01:49.242
desperately pleads

00:01:49.242 --> 00:01:50.610
with volunteer rescuers

00:01:50.610 --> 00:01:52.645
to search for her husband, Kadir.

00:01:53.246 --> 00:01:54.080
He's buried,

00:01:54.080 --> 00:01:56.116
she says, in their corner apartment,

00:01:56.116 --> 00:01:58.551
which is somewhere under this rubble

00:02:02.255 --> 00:02:03.490
They try to console her,

00:02:03.490 --> 00:02:05.892
but this mother of twins wants action,

00:02:05.892 --> 00:02:07.093
not words.

00:02:07.093 --> 00:02:09.362
This gives you this picture

00:02:09.362 --> 00:02:10.930
now to get older. You are.

00:02:10.930 --> 00:02:12.398
There is nobody out there.

00:02:12.398 --> 00:02:14.267
It's been six days.

00:02:14.267 --> 00:02:16.069
I'm waiting here with my twins

00:02:16.069 --> 00:02:18.071
standing in the cold.

00:02:18.071 --> 00:02:20.006
She says she's been asking anyone

00:02:20.006 --> 00:02:21.975
who will listen to dig her husband out.

00:02:21.975 --> 00:02:23.576
But for six days,

00:02:23.576 --> 00:02:24.477
she says officials

00:02:24.477 --> 00:02:25.245
kept telling her

00:02:25.245 --> 00:02:26.246
they needed permission

00:02:26.246 --> 00:02:26.980
from the government

00:02:26.980 --> 00:02:28.781
to start on her building.

00:02:28.781 --> 00:02:30.083
I'm still here.

00:02:30.083 --> 00:02:31.818
I want my husband back,

00:02:31.818 --> 00:02:33.453
even if he's not alive.

00:02:34.787 --> 00:02:36.156
She may have accepted his

00:02:36.156 --> 00:02:37.891
death, but can't go on

00:02:37.891 --> 00:02:40.059
without seeing her husband's body

00:02:40.059 --> 00:02:43.263
removed from this hellscape

00:02:46.232 --> 00:02:48.735
My life, my blood, my everything.

00:02:48.735 --> 00:02:50.570
My best friend in life.

00:02:50.570 --> 00:02:52.705
He left me with my twins here alone.

00:02:53.706 --> 00:02:56.142
While she waits for the realities

00:02:56.142 --> 00:02:59.245
of her husband's death here in this area

00:02:59.245 --> 00:03:02.348
where you see enormous piles of rubble.

00:03:02.882 --> 00:03:04.184
These are different buildings,

00:03:04.184 --> 00:03:06.152
but you can't really distinguish them

00:03:06.152 --> 00:03:08.588
because there's just so much destruction.

00:03:09.055 --> 00:03:11.558
There have been signs of life.

00:03:11.558 --> 00:03:14.194
A child was found here alive

00:03:14.594 --> 00:03:18.264
after a week in the rubble.

00:03:18.398 --> 00:03:20.667
Nurses comfort the girl who they think is

00:03:20.667 --> 00:03:22.402
three or four years old.

00:03:22.402 --> 00:03:25.572
She's dehydrated and in shock, but alive

00:03:28.441 --> 00:03:32.145
This is the moment she was rescued.

00:03:32.278 --> 00:03:33.580
Her exhausted little body

00:03:33.580 --> 00:03:34.414
pulled from under

00:03:34.414 --> 00:03:36.950
the seemingly endless mountains of rubble

00:03:36.950 --> 00:03:37.817
and her time

00:03:39.852 --> 00:03:42.822
mother was still motionless and

00:03:42.822 --> 00:03:45.024
she was rushed to the makeshift hospital

00:03:45.024 --> 00:03:46.059
set up in the parking

00:03:46.059 --> 00:03:47.994
lot of the actual hospital

00:03:47.994 --> 00:03:50.129
that was evacuated after the earthquake

00:03:50.396 --> 00:03:51.497
hit Candy.

00:03:51.497 --> 00:03:53.666
When she first arrived as a mother,

00:03:53.666 --> 00:03:56.002
I felt that she was like my own daughter.

00:03:56.035 --> 00:03:58.004
This nurse says

00:03:58.338 --> 00:03:59.806
she's cracking up the staff.

00:03:59.806 --> 00:04:00.807
She's talking.

00:04:00.807 --> 00:04:01.908
When we walked in,

00:04:01.908 --> 00:04:03.209
the toddler had managed

00:04:03.209 --> 00:04:05.011
to make the nurses laugh.

00:04:05.011 --> 00:04:07.180
Relieved she could talk a bit.

00:04:07.180 --> 00:04:09.048
What is it that she said that made

00:04:09.048 --> 00:04:09.782
you all laugh?

00:04:09.782 --> 00:04:11.451
She made all the nurses laugh.

00:04:11.451 --> 00:04:12.285
I mean,

00:04:12.852 --> 00:04:13.319
Mama,

00:04:13.319 --> 00:04:15.288
I meant the word that made all the nurses

00:04:15.288 --> 00:04:16.389
laugh was Mama.

00:04:16.389 --> 00:04:17.590
And I'm hungry.

00:04:17.590 --> 00:04:19.892
I want to eat something

00:04:20.393 --> 00:04:21.995
What does that do to your heart?

00:04:21.995 --> 00:04:24.197
When she said Mama cried.

00:04:24.197 --> 00:04:26.299
I felt a great pulse in my heart,

00:04:26.299 --> 00:04:27.600
she says.

00:04:27.767 --> 00:04:29.135
No one knew her name.

00:04:29.135 --> 00:04:31.471
And when they asked, she said, Dada.

00:04:31.671 --> 00:04:33.072
It turns out this

00:04:33.072 --> 00:04:34.974
toddler does not speak Turkish.

00:04:34.974 --> 00:04:36.542
She speaks Arabic.

00:04:36.542 --> 00:04:39.379
Rescuers later tell us she's Syrian.

00:04:40.980 --> 00:04:41.814
Here we go.

00:04:41.814 --> 00:04:42.348
Sara, I know

00:04:42.348 --> 00:04:43.182
you've been reporting on here.

00:04:43.182 --> 00:04:43.983
Do we know anything else

00:04:43.983 --> 00:04:45.985
about the little girl

00:04:48.421 --> 00:04:48.721
You know,

00:04:48.721 --> 00:04:50.189
we went to the area

00:04:50.189 --> 00:04:51.991
where they pulled her out

00:04:51.991 --> 00:04:54.060
and there was no one left.

00:04:54.127 --> 00:04:55.995
What we do know is

00:04:55.995 --> 00:04:57.397
perhaps what's going to happen

00:04:57.397 --> 00:04:59.432
is when she is fully treated,

00:04:59.432 --> 00:05:00.633
she is going to find out

00:05:00.633 --> 00:05:01.901
that they have not yet

00:05:01.901 --> 00:05:03.202
been able to find

00:05:03.202 --> 00:05:04.804
either of her parents

00:05:04.804 --> 00:05:06.472
at this point in time.

00:05:06.472 --> 00:05:08.574
We are now in the eighth day.

00:05:08.574 --> 00:05:09.709
They do not think that

00:05:09.709 --> 00:05:10.610
they have survived.

00:05:10.610 --> 00:05:12.912
So this little girl may indeed

00:05:13.246 --> 00:05:14.247
become an orphan

00:05:14.247 --> 00:05:15.882
after all that she has been through.

00:05:15.882 --> 00:05:16.649
Caitlin

00:05:16.683 --> 00:05:17.750
And just the thought

00:05:17.750 --> 00:05:19.185
that she's not the only one.

00:05:19.185 --> 00:05:21.154
There are so many other children

00:05:21.154 --> 00:05:22.322
living through that same thing.

00:05:22.322 --> 00:05:23.022
Sara Sidner,

00:05:23.022 --> 00:05:24.157
you're live in southern Turkey.

00:05:24.157 --> 00:05:25.358
Thank you for being there this morning.

